# Offline pin notes — gpw-xdm-kpoint-forces

## Policy

CP2K 2026.1 stock `PAIR_POTENTIAL TYPE` is only
`DFTD2|DFTD3|DFTD3(BJ)|DFTD4` (`input_cp2k_xc.F` usage string) — **no**
`TYPE XDM`. Binary checked offline:

```text
cp2k.psmp  version 2026.1  Source code revision git:5e54ba2
  via /nobackup/proj/disk/teoroo/personal/jicli594/work/cp2k/install/env.sh
```

Canonical density-dependent XDM oracles are postg / critic2 / QE
`xdm_dispersion`. Atomiverse ships the **free-atom** foothold (geometry-only
multipole moments + CRC α) with dual pure-Python lattice sum + analytic
gradient. Fair wall is therefore **perf_exempt** — never fake
`oracle: cp2k`. Same policy as `gpw-xdm-forces` / `gpw-xdm-kpoint-stress` /
`gpw-xdm-ice`.

## Residual closed

Dedicated multi-k ionic-force pin for free-atom XDM. Product multi-k
`assemble_gpw_forces_kpoints` already folds `xdm` (same geometry-only
`xdm_pbe` call as Γ); this slug hard-gates dual pure-Python energy/force
pins + multi-k product wiring (H₂ 1×1×2).

## Pins

### Water dimer — free-atom XDM (QE NC-PBE a1/a2, rcut 50 Å)

Geometry (Å):

```
O  0.000000  0.000000  0.000000
H  0.758602  0.000000  0.504284
H  0.758602  0.000000 -0.504284
O  3.000000  0.000000  0.000000
H  3.758602  0.000000  0.504284
H  3.758602  0.000000 -0.504284
```

Å→Bohr: `1/0.52917720859` (ATV).

- Isolated: E_disp = −2.1020435998516220×10⁻³ Ha
- Periodic: E_disp = −2.1148157612879029×10⁻³ Ha

Force dual-gate (never live in ctest):

```text
max |F_product − F_fd(h=1e-5)| ≤ 1e-6 Ha/Bohr
|sum F| ≤ 1e-8 Ha/Bohr
```

Isolated free-atom sample F [Ha/Bohr] (ATV order O H H O H H) — bit-class
match to dual pure-Python (same numbers as `gpw-xdm-forces`):

| Atom | Fx | Fy | Fz |
| ---- | -- | -- | -- |
| O0 | +1.6875829936003448e-04 | 0 | 0 |
| H0 | +6.9736686381575340e-05 | 0 | −1.3172272218329521e-05 |
| H1 | +6.9736686381575340e-05 | 0 | +1.3172272218329521e-05 |
| O1 | −1.1378113807647229e-04 | 0 | 0 |
| H2 | −9.7225267023356434e-05 | 0 | −1.5448899346549854e-05 |
| H3 | −9.7225267023356434e-05 | 0 | +1.5448899346549854e-05 |

Provenance: XDM is geometry-only — independent of the electronic
Monkhorst–Pack mesh — so the unstrained energy/force pins are bit-identical
to `gpw-xdm-forces` / `gpw-xdm-ice`. The multi-k product path must still
reproduce the wiring gate because `assemble_gpw_forces_kpoints` rebuilds
\(F_{\mathrm{XDM}}\) after the k-summed electronic assembly.

### H₂ multi-k wiring

- Cell 12³ Bohr, k-mesh 1×1×2, PADE + DZV-GTH-PADE, bond 1.0 Bohr.
- `xdm=true`, periodic free-atom lattice sum (rcut 50 Å).
- Gate: \(F^{k+\mathrm{XDM}}-F^{k}\approx F_{\mathrm{XDM}}^{\mathrm{geom}}\)
  to 1e-8 Ha/Bohr.

See `regressions/gpw/gpw-xdm-kpoint-forces/REFERENCE.md`.
